Guard the layer-shell idle ids where they are used, as where they are declared

set_monitor_idle_id and monitor_removed_idle_id are members of
TerminalWindowDropdown only when HAVE_GTK_LAYER_SHELL is defined -- the
declaration at the top of the file is inside that #ifdef, as is every other
use of them.  The finalize function is the exception: it cancels both idle
sources unconditionally, so a build without gtk-layer-shell does not compile:

  'TerminalWindowDropdown' has no member named 'set_monitor_idle_id'

gtk-layer-shell is a Wayland library and this is an X11-only system, so it is
not built here and the option is off.  The fix is the guard the rest of the
file already uses; the sources being cancelled cannot exist when the fields do
not.

--- a/terminal/terminal-window-dropdown.c
+++ b/terminal/terminal-window-dropdown.c
@@ -567,11 +567,13 @@
   if (dropdown->animation_timeout_id != 0)
     g_source_remove (dropdown->animation_timeout_id);
 
+#ifdef HAVE_GTK_LAYER_SHELL
   if (dropdown->set_monitor_idle_id != 0)
     g_source_remove (dropdown->set_monitor_idle_id);
 
   if (dropdown->monitor_removed_idle_id != 0)
     g_source_remove (dropdown->monitor_removed_idle_id);
+#endif
 
   if (dropdown->status_icon != NULL)
     g_object_unref (G_OBJECT (dropdown->status_icon));
